# Manual GitHub pushes only

- Never run `git push`, `git push --force`, or create/update GitHub PRs that imply an immediate production deploy **unless the user clearly asks to push** (e.g. “push to GitHub”, “deploy”, “ship this”, “run git push”).
- Local commits, branches, and `git status` / `git diff` are fine without asking.
- Netlify production follows GitHub; keeping pushes explicit protects viewers (e.g. Kevin) from seeing half-finished work.
